---
title: Narrative
sidebar:
  order: 8
---

A narrative is your field journal. Use it to record observations, decisions,
and other context that may not fit in a specimen or event record.

## Creating a narrative

{% steps %}

1. Open the Narrative page from the navigation bar.
2. Select `+` or `Create narrative`.
3. Enter the `Date` and, optionally, the `Time`.
4. Select a `Site`. The site name is displayed automatically from the site's
   locality information.

    {% aside type="note" %}
    Create at least one site on the [Sites page](/en/usages/sites) before
    selecting a site for a narrative.
    {% /aside %}

5. Select the `Writer` from the personnel assigned to the project.
6. Enter the narrative text.

{% /steps %}

The date and time are stored separately. If you enter a time without a date,
NAHPU uses the current date.

## Writing and previewing text

Narrative text supports Markdown. Use the `Preview` and `Edit` controls above
the text field to switch between writing and rendered views.

## Adding media

Attach media to a narrative from the camera, device gallery, or file picker.
Narrative media is included when the project is transferred and can also be
included in exports where narrative media is selected.

## Searching and managing narratives

Use the search button in the Narrative app bar to filter narrative entries.
Use the page controls to move between entries. The menu for the selected entry
provides these deletion actions:

- **Delete narrative** - Delete the selected narrative and its associated
  media.
- **Delete all narrative** - Delete every narrative in the active project.

Deletion is permanent. Export or back up the project first if the entries may
be needed later.
